popupAttrT -- popups stroke 5 (SEQ 775, assigned by Clod, 2026-11-25; Tony's ruling 1 on docs/popupsRecon.md and his two of
2026-11-24): popup:=aForm as an attribute, and OK and Cancel through the pour return link (stroke 4b). Tester's shape; no
window is shown; every click is a real mouse-up. pqHost pours PqThree as derived rows (name, value, dESCRIPTIONs' words) and
its poured field carries popup:=pqPop: the pour knows nothing of the popup. Only pqTwo has words. pqPop shows the member it
was opened on ({each.taG}, {dESCRIPTIONs.each}), has one row that picks its own text, an OK and a Cancel. PqThree pours in
name order: pqOne, pqThree, pqTwo.
Read: the click and popup lines; the popup's target (PQ-TARGET: the hit cell, the member, the member's registry, and the
cell's pour address read when the popup opened); what the popup's own each is (PQ-EACH, read by a click in the popup); and
dESCRIPTIONs' three entries, pqText's text in the definition, and how many popups are open (PQ-STATE).
Q-0  as defined.
Q-1  a click in pqTwo's description cell opens pqPop AT THAT CELL; the popup's each is pqTwo and its words are drawn (13
     characters); Cancel.
Q-2  THE EMPTY ADDRESSED CELL: pqOne has no description, so its cell shows nothing; it is selected (not only room: it has an
     address) and the popup opens on it, each pqOne, make yes; the popup's page differs from Q-1's (no words to draw).
     fresh words picked, OK: the entry is MADE through the link and the line says so; pqHost laid out again.
Q-3  CANCEL THROUGH THE LINK: pqThree's empty cell, a pick, Cancel: nothing written, no entry made.
Q-4  an entry that exists (pqTwo): written, nothing made.
Q-5  READ-ONLY: opened on pqOne's name cell, a pick, OK: it says read-only with the reason, writes nothing, closes.
Q-6  NOT POURED, AND THE CLIMB: pqRoom is only room under pqBox, which carries popup:=pqPop. Nothing is selected (the negative
     control for Q-2: an empty cell with no address still climbs); the popup opens from pqBox, on the cell that was hit.
Q-7  a plain field carrying popup:= itself: a pick and OK write its text in the definition, as stroke 3 does (no link).
Q-8  only room with no popup above it: nothing selected, nothing fired, no popup.
Q-9  THE CUSTOMER: colorList's clRows carries popup:=colorWords. A point in radialGreen's row opens colorWords showing that
     colour's name and words; its OK closes it, nothing picked, nothing written.
